NAME CIA
IO_STRING CIA X
TYPE POLYMER
AA UNK
## S-carboxymethyl-L-cysteine  (C-IAA: cysteine alkylated with iodoacetic acid)
## Side chain: CB - SG - CD(H2) - CE(=OZ1)(OZ2)
##
## Derived from l-ncaa/amino-ethyl-cysteine.params (B63), which shares the exact
## CB-SG-CD-CE skeleton and whose backbone/ICOOR tree and polymer connect records
## are reused unchanged. Only the side-chain tip differs: B63 terminates in an
## amine (NZ + 3H), CIA terminates in a carboxyl (CE retyped to COO, plus OZ1/OZ2).
## Carboxyl atom types, charges and internal geometry are taken from GLU's
## CD/OE1/OE2. Rosetta ships no S-carboxymethyl-cysteine; the other six ncAAs in
## this project are database built-ins (BCS, A48, C00, C01, ABA, NLU).
ATOM  N   Nbb  NH1  -0.59
ATOM  CA  CAbb CT1  -0.07
ATOM  C   CObb C    0.64
ATOM  O   OCbb O    -0.53
ATOM  CB  CH2  CT2  -0.16
ATOM  SG  S    S    -0.14
ATOM  CD  CH2  CT2  -0.16
ATOM  CE  COO  CC   0.43
## OZ1/OZ2 carry -0.735 rather than GLU's -0.5948. Reason: the B63 template this
## file is derived from is itself charge-imbalanced (+0.870 for a formally +1
## residue), and inheriting that left CIA at -0.710 for a formally -1 carboxylate
## -- a ~29% electrostatics deficit on the one group whose interaction with KIX we
## are trying to measure. The excess is absorbed onto the two carboxylate oxygens,
## which carry the formal negative charge, bringing the net to exactly -1.000
## (matching canonical GLU/ASP). CE keeps GLU's carboxyl-carbon charge.
ATOM  OZ1 OOC  OC   -0.735
ATOM  OZ2 OOC  OC   -0.735
ATOM  H   HNbb H    0.45
ATOM  HA  Hapo HB   0.12
ATOM 1HB  Hapo HA   0.12
ATOM 2HB  Hapo HA   0.12
ATOM 1HD  Hapo HA   0.12
ATOM 2HD  Hapo HA   0.12
BOND  CA   N
BOND  N    H
BOND  CA   HA
BOND  CA   CB
BOND  CA   C
BOND  C    O
BOND  SG   CB
BOND  CB  1HB
BOND  CB  2HB
BOND  SG   CD
BOND  CD  1HD
BOND  CD  2HD
BOND  CE   CD
BOND  CE   OZ1
BOND  CE   OZ2
LOWER_CONNECT N
UPPER_CONNECT C
CHI 1  N    CA   CB   SG
CHI 2  CA   CB   SG   CD
CHI 3  CB   SG   CD   CE
CHI 4  SG   CD   CE   OZ1
NBR_ATOM  CB
NBR_RADIUS 7.693346
FIRST_SIDECHAIN_ATOM  CB
